      {
        "id": 39610,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-07T22:24:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Nah, there's another one I know of. &nbsp;Experimental Mutagen and a sufficiently buff-ed Expatriette with Hair-Trigger Reflexes. &nbsp;The Rat comes in, gets killed, goes back to the discard, and Experimental Mutagen continues bringing rats from the discard. &nbsp;As stated above, the \"first time\" or \"once\" solution has usually been suggested to solve this (i.e. Experimental Mutagen brings all rats back \"once\").</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Before it was an oddity, but when you combine this particular loop with Akash'bhuta.....*shudder*.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:13:20.808Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
